# Chapter 34: Standard Document, Data & Physics Wire Formats

Cluster features unified, zero-dependency domain file formats engineered for high-density systems and AI applications:
- **`.cld` (Cluster Document)**: Markdown and document AST format (`std/cld.cl`)
- **`.clb` (Cluster Binary Bundle)**: Zero-overhead binary package archive (`std/clb.cl`)
- **`.cls` (Cluster Schema)**: Type contract and interface schema validation (`std/cls.cl`)
- **`.clw` (Cluster World)**: 3D spatial voxel physics and world state (`std/clw.cl`)

These standards allow writing games, static sites, database layers, and distributed networking tools purely in Cluster without external protocol libraries.
